===== SECTION 36 (out/.vo_Weapons_That_Succeeded_for_the_Wrong_Reasons_Explained/parts/sec_035.mp3) =====
The night that made it immortal came later that same year. For 25 hours, the British pounded Fort McHenry guarding Baltimore Harbor with shells and Congreve rockets, and it achieved almost nothing. Just four Americans died in the whole bombardment, and the fort held. But a man watching from a ship, a lawyer named Francis Scott Key turned that long night of red streaks into a poem, the rocket's red glare.
