At the Battle of Rassowice, Kostjusko sent them straight at the Russian artillery, the deadliest thing on the field. About 300 Sithemen ran across open ground into the guns and took them, capturing 12 cannon. One of them, a peasant named Vojek-Govatsky, is said to have put out a cannon's burning fuse with his own cap before it could fire and became a national hero overnight.
